      "problem": "Sketch the graph of $y=|x|-3$.",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x|+a$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x|-3$ has $a=-3.$ Therefore, it is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $3$ units *down*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/7266634257d662b0af75fdb80d402acaa779df2ed4b62fc43c074a7f4f902de0.png)",
